Here's a compact visual report window summarizing why an OpenCloset eval harness matters:

<transient-window id="b7e41a" title="OpenCloset Eval Harness â Why It Matters" summary="Three-bullet rationale and a compact scorecard for the OpenCloset eval harness.">
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>OpenCloset Eval Harness â Why It Matters</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --border: #2a2d3a;
    --accent: #6ee7b7;
    --accent2: #7dd3fc;
    --text: #e2e4ea;
    --muted: #9ca3af;
    --gold: #fbbf24;
    --red: #f87171;
    --green: #4ade80;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    padding: 24px;
    min-height: 100vh;
  }
  .header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .header h1 {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .header .tag {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #0f1117;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 99px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .bullets {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .bullet {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
  }
  .bullet .icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .bullet:nth-child(1) .icon { background: #1e3a2f; color: var(--green); }
  .bullet:nth-child(2) .icon { background: #1e293b; color: var(--accent2); }
  .bullet:nth-child(3) .icon { background: #3b2e1e; color: var(--gold); }
  .bullet h3 {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 3px;
  }
  .bullet p {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .scorecard {
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
  }
  .scorecard h2 {
    font-size: 12px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .score-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .score-item {
    text-align: center;
  }
  .score-item .label {
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .score-item .value {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .bar-track {
    height: 4px;
    background: var(--border);
    border-radius: 2px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .bar-fill {
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 2px;
    transition: width 0.6s ease;
  }
  .score-item:nth-child(1) .value { color: var(--green); }
  .score-item:nth-child(1) .bar-fill { background: var(--green); width: 92%; }
  .score-item:nth-child(2) .value { color: var(--accent2); }
  .score-item:nth-child(2) .bar-fill { background: var(--accent2); width: 87%; }
  .score-item:nth-child(3) .value { color: var(--gold); }
  .score-item:nth-child(3) .bar-fill { background: var(--gold); width: 78%; }
  .score-item:nth-child(4) .value { color: var(--accent); }
  .score-item:nth-child(4) .bar-fill { background: var(--accent); width: 95%; }
  .footer {
    margin-top: 16px;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="header">
    <h1>OpenCloset Eval Harness</h1>
    <span class="tag">Why It Matters</span>
  </div>

  <div class="bullets">
    <div class="bullet">
      <div class="icon">1</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Reproducible Quality Signals</h3>
        <p>Turns subjective "does it look right?" into repeatable, version-controlled benchmarks so every PR can be measured against the same bar.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="bullet">
      <div class="icon">2</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Regression Guardrails</h3>
        <p>Catches wardrobe-graph bugs, style-mismatch drift, and outfit-recommendation regressions before they ship â not after users complain.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="bullet">
      <div class="icon">3</div>
      <div>
        <h3>Model-Agnostic Comparison</h3>
        <p>Same test suite, multiple backends. Swap LLMs or ranking strategies and see the delta in seconds, not weeks of manual review.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="scorecard">
    <h2>Scorecard â Current Harness Health</h2>
    <div class="score-grid">
      <div class="score-item">
        <div class="label">Coverage</div>
        <div class="value">92%</div>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill"></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="score-item">
        <div class="label">Stability</div>
        <div class="value">87%</div>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill"></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="score-item">
        <div class="label">Signal</div>
        <div class="value">78%</div>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill"></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="score-item">
        <div class="label">Speed</div>
        <div class="value">95%</div>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill"></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="footer">OpenCloset Eval Harness Â· Generated 2026-05-09</div>
</body>
</html>
</transient-window>

The window gives you three concrete reasons the harness matters â reproducible quality signals, regression guardrails, and model-agnostic comparison â plus a compact scorecard tracking coverage, stability, signal quality, and run speed. The scorecard values are illustrative placeholders; swap them in once the harness produces real metrics.
